  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-forensic art direction, decisive white/red headline, restrained cyan/green accents, and consistent card styling. However, desktop feels under-filled with excessive dead space; tablet has awkwardly floating connector lines and an overlong vertical composition; mobile becomes a repetitive card stack with weakened narrative flow. Tiny, low-contrast mono labels reduce refinement, while the desktop header’s oversized ghost wordmark and edge-clipped navigation look visually unresolved.",
    "fix": "Tighten desktop and tablet spacing, anchor connectors precisely to cards, and create a more compact mobile evidence timeline. Increase secondary-label size/contrast and resolve header clipping/ghost-wordmark interference across breakpoints.",
